<div class="callout">
  <h2>Do You Actually Need a Subscription?</h2>
  <p>No — a Cookidoo membership isn't mandatory to use the TM7. Without one, you can still cook manually (setting time, temperature, and speed yourself) and use whatever recipes ship pre-loaded on the machine. But Cookidoo is what actually speeds up the whole process — the automatic guided steps, meal planner, and shopping lists save real time versus cooking manually — and at $89 CAD/year, it's worth it for the 100,000+ recipe library alone.</p>
</div>

<p>You can also browse Cookidoo's recipe library from a web browser or the app without owning a TM7 at all — you just won't be able to send a recipe to a machine to run it, since Guided Cooking only works once Cookidoo is paired with a Thermomix.</p>

